gcmove 1 fps:30
build {
}
# SWORD GRIP: a firm right-hand grip on a handle, as shipped in PresetSlash_Keys.gcmove (21 Nov 2026), on the BlueEdge MetaHuman sword body.
# Guide: HOLDING-A-SWORD.md beside this file.
#
# THE METHOD (owner 21 Nov: "three poses, one by one, first is hand open, second is four fingers closed, third is thumb on top"):
#   1. the SEAT by geometry: the handle placed so the OPEN hand touches it (0-2 mm) with nothing inside, measured, not swept;
#   2. the FOUR FINGERS by plain values, each segment touching the handle within the flesh's 3.5 mm;
#   3. the THUMB by plain values on top.
# No collision forms and no collision(self, $Grip) slide: the build's own final audit reports any pass-through and refuses it.
# The values below are FITTED for the BlueEdge handle (3.3 x 2.64 cm rounded) on this body; another prop or body needs its own fit
# (HOLDING-A-SWORD.md section 2, the scripts in Saved/Research/MOVE-PARAM1/seatfix/).
#
# HOW TO USE (paste route, the one that was measured): copy everything from "Grip = surface" down to the last preset into your
# own .gcmove, after your header and before your clips, then in EVERY key write, in this order:
#     $Hand(wrist=-30, wrist_side=2, left=false)   $SwordSeat   $SwordFist   $SwordThumb
# The import route (presets:<this file>) is NOT verified. Use paste.
#
# WHAT YOU NEED FIRST (the guide's section 1): palm_r (the carrier the handle rides) with the hand's velocity/accel/ramp, and
# thumb_opp_r / thumb_roll_r with thumb_01_r's references. BlueEdge_20261013/MetaHumanSwordRig.gcrig has them. palm_r's
# translation must play (SK_BlueEdgeBody_Skeleton retargeting palm_r = Animation, 21 Nov) or the seat's shift is discarded.

Sword = surface(part=Sword)
Grip = surface(part=Sword, solid=collision)

# 1. THE SEAT (pose 1, hand open): turned 22 about palm_r X (the handle along the finger-root line), 4 about Y (the pommel end into
# the heel), moved 2.124 cm in the turned frame toward the finger roots and the blade and 1.1 mm into the palm. Open hand, mm of gap:
# heel 0.2, index root 0.0, pinky root 0.2, middle metacarpal 0.9, ring root 2.1, thenar 2.3, index metacarpal 2.4, ring metacarpal 3.2,
# middle root 5.0; none inside. Same in every key. With wrist=-30, wrist_side=2 the handle is 71.9 deg to the forearm (the square look).
SwordSeat = pose() {
  swing(palm_r,axis=X,by=22)
  swing(palm_r,axis=Y,by=4)
  shift(palm_r,axis=(-0.0789,0.9193,0.3856),by=2.124)
}

# 2. THE FOUR FINGERS (pose 2), plain values fitted so each segment touches the handle 0.5-2.5 mm into the skin, spread closed
# (index -6, ring +4, pinky +8; + is toward the thumb). Contact mm knuckle/middle/tip: index -2.3/+2.9/-2.4, middle -0.6/-0.5/-1.1,
# ring -0.9/-2.2/-0.7, pinky -2.4/-1.2/-2.0.
SwordFist = pose() {
  swing(index_01_r,axis=fold,by=-2)
  swing(index_02_r,axis=fold,by=54)
  swing(index_03_r,axis=fold,by=13)
  swing(index_01_r,axis=side,by=-6)
  swing(middle_01_r,axis=fold,by=15)
  swing(middle_02_r,axis=fold,by=43)
  swing(middle_03_r,axis=fold,by=20.5)
  swing(ring_01_r,axis=fold,by=15)
  swing(ring_02_r,axis=fold,by=33)
  swing(ring_03_r,axis=fold,by=33.8)
  swing(ring_01_r,axis=side,by=4)
  swing(pinky_01_r,axis=fold,by=0)
  swing(pinky_02_r,axis=fold,by=20)
  swing(pinky_03_r,axis=fold,by=10)
  swing(pinky_01_r,axis=side,by=8)
}

# 3. THE THUMB ON TOP (pose 3), plain values: its middle segment and tip rest on the handle and the tip on the middle fingertip.
# KNOWN GAP: with the handle at the finger roots the index's first segment lies over the handle top, so the tip stops on it 2.7 cm
# short of the index middle segment (the iaido photo's place). thumb_opp_r works -12.7..77 on this body (not the declared -30..60).
SwordThumb = pose() {
  swing(thumb_01_r,axis=fold,by=-30)
  swing(thumb_01_r,axis=twist,by=17)
  swing(thumb_opp_r,axis=fold,by=47.5)
  swing(thumb_roll_r,axis=twist,by=16)
  swing(thumb_02_r,axis=fold,by=-10)
  swing(thumb_03_r,axis=fold,by=5)
}

# Example key (one frame; keep the arm, body and wrist lines of your own key):
#   Cock = clip(frames=1) {
#     ...your feet, hips, back, head, $ArmReach(...)...
#     $Hand(wrist=-30, wrist_side=2, left=false)
#     $SwordSeat  $SwordFist  $SwordThumb
#   }
